  "id": "Compound::DB01085 - Gene::1131",
  "verbalization": "Pilocarpine, a muscarinic acetylcholine receptor agonist, is shown to bind to Chrm2, which is involved in the activation of muscarinic acetylcholine receptors. This binding leads to the participation of Chrm2 in various receptor activities, including G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity and G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptor activity. These activities ultimately result in the participation of Chrm3, suggesting a mechanistic link between Pilocarpine and Chrm3 through the activation of muscarinic receptors. The evidence supports a pathway where Pilocarpine modulates muscarinic receptor function, leading to the activation of Chrm3. The consistent binding to Chrm2 and the involvement of Chrm3 in receptor activities indicate that Pilocarpine may exert its effects through a well-defined mechanism involving muscarinic receptor activation. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Chrm3 in the downstream effects of Pilocarpine, emphasizing the importance of muscarinic receptor signaling in the observed interactions.",
